 type system overhaul done for 1.2.0b3. Below is the error and attached is a file used to produce the error below.  The code includes two custom functions (month and add_months) with implementations for both oracle and sqlite, but have only included the oracle bits.\r\n\r\n[error_script.txt](https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/files/3686730/error_script.txt)\r\n\r\n> sqlalchemy.exc.DatabaseError: (cx_Oracle.DatabaseError) ORA-00932: inconsistent datatypes: expected DATE got CHAR [SQL: \"SELECT spend_track.track_id AS spend_track_track_id, spend_track.campaign_id AS spend_track_campaign_id, spend_track.start_date AS spend_track_start_date, spend_track.end_date AS spend_track_end_date, spend_track.through_date AS spend_track_through_date\r\n> FROM spend_track\r\n> WHERE :param_1 = spend_track.campaign_id AND CASE WHEN (:param_2 != :type_1) THEN CASE WHEN (CASE WHEN (:param_3 IS NOT NULL) THEN (SELECT bill.invoice_date\r\n> FROM bill\r\n> WHERE bill.bill_id = :param_3) ELSE :param_4 END IS NOT NULL) THEN TRUNC(CASE WHEN (:param_3 IS NOT NULL) THEN (SELECT bill.invoice_date\r\n> FROM bill\r\n> WHERE bill.bill_id = :param_3) ELSE :param_4 END, 'MONTH') ELSE TRUNC(ADD_MONTHS(:param_5, (SELECT division.bill_month_offset\r\n> FROM division, insertion_order, campaign\r\n> WHERE division.division_id = insertion_order.division_id AND insertion_order.order_id = campaign.order_id AND campaign.campaign_id = :param_1)), 'MONTH') END ELSE TRUNC(:param_5, 'MONTH') END = TRUNC(spend_track.through_date, 'MONTH') AND :param_2 = :type_2 ORDER BY spend_track.through_date\"] [parameters: {'param_1': 16807, 'param_2': 'D', 'type_1': 'D', 'param_3': None, 'param_4': None, 'param_5': datetime.date(2019, 10, 7), 'type_2': 'D'}]","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy